# Energy panel

A full `energy` tile is an edge-to-edge page of the solar / grid / battery / home diagram from Home Assistant's energy preferences (`energy/get_prefs`). The 2×2 energy tile still draws the same diagram inside card chrome via `energyFlow(..., compact)`.

## Wiring

- Catalogue kind `energy` in `_kinds.yaml`: sizes `[2x2, full]`, card `energy`.
- `OTHER_TILE_KINDS` includes `energy`. Other tiles click/drag uses `kindSource('energy')` → `{ kind: 'energy', full: true }` so the library opens a page even though 2×2 is first in the catalogue.
- `Tile.edgeToEdge()` and `Tiles.kt` dispatch full energy to `energyPanel` (`panels/energy/EnergyPanel.kt`), which fills `Role.PAGE` and calls `energyFlow` with `compact = false`. `hasOwnTaps` includes `energy` so the page has no default card hold (entity nodes still open history on long-press).
- Non-full energy tiles keep the card path in `SpecialtyTiles.energyFlow`.
- Data: `RenderDataRepository.energy()` / `EnergyPrefs` when any tile kind is `energy`.

## Editor

`GridMockup.vue` draws a static solar/grid/battery/home layout for `isEnergyPanel`. `TileDrawer.vue` treats full energy as edge-to-edge (no card chrome fields).

## Verify

```bash
./gradlew :server:detekt :server:test --tests '*RenderTest.aFullEnergyTileIsTheEnergyPage'
cd editor && npm run lint && npm test -- --run src/model/otherTiles.test.ts
```
